# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock is intentionally tracked, not ignored: kube-shim is a binary,
# not a library, so a committed lock file is what makes the release build
# reproducible (and, since PR #9, matches what SLSA provenance actually
# claims about the build). See docs/RELEASING.md.

